0..80 Comment "//! A bridge `Bridge[.A = A](a, b)` relates two points of `A` parametrically, as"
81..111 Comment "//! the bridge fold reads `A`."
112..115 Comment "//!"
116..193 Comment "//! A path identifies its endpoints, and a bridge only relates them. A bridge"
194..271 Comment "//! at the universe is a relation between two types, and one at a type former"
272..348 Comment "//! lifts the relations of its parts. A bridge has no reflexivity, transport"
349..378 Comment "//! or eliminator of its own."
379..382 Comment "//!"
383..462 Comment "//! An introduction checked at a bridge checks at the fibre the fold reads from"
463..540 Comment "//! the carrier and the endpoints. The fold reads a list cell by cell, a base"
541..617 Comment "//! type or a sum as its identity, and a function code by extensionality. An"
618..673 Comment "//! atom stating an identity system bears its relation."
674..677 Comment "//!"
678..749 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/identity/bridge.gandr` — the bridges refused"
750..797 Comment "//! - see: #3519 — the model laws of the fold"
798..874 Comment "//! - cites: [Cavallo-2021-internal_parametricity_cubical_type_theory], § 3"
875..878 Comment "//!"
879..1052 Comment "//! [Cavallo-2021-internal_parametricity_cubical_type_theory]: https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-17(4:5)2021 \"Cavallo and Harper, Internal parametricity for cubical type theory\""
